## Master Prompt — Employee Management System (ASP.NET Core MVC)

```
You are a senior ASP.NET Core developer. Build a complete, production-ready 
Employee Management System as a single ASP.NET Core MVC project (.NET 8).

---

TECH STACK:
- ASP.NET Core 8 MVC
- Entity Framework Core (SQL Server / SQLite)
- Identity Framework (Authentication + Role-based Authorization)
- Bootstrap 5 + custom CSS
- JavaScript (vanilla, no frameworks)
- Razor Views (.cshtml)

---

PROJECT STRUCTURE:
EmployeeManagementSystem/
├── Controllers/
│   ├── AccountController.cs
│   ├── DashboardController.cs
│   ├── EmployeeController.cs
│   ├── DepartmentController.cs
│   ├── AttendanceController.cs
│   ├── LeaveController.cs
│   └── PayrollController.cs
├── Models/
│   ├── Employee.cs
│   ├── Department.cs
│   ├── Attendance.cs
│   ├── LeaveRequest.cs
│   └── Payroll.cs
├── ViewModels/
│   ├── LoginViewModel.cs
│   ├── RegisterViewModel.cs
│   ├── EmployeeViewModel.cs
│   └── DashboardViewModel.cs
├── Data/
│   └── ApplicationDbContext.cs
├── Views/
│   ├── Shared/
│   │   ├── _Layout.cshtml
│   │   └── _Sidebar.cshtml
│   ├── Dashboard/
│   ├── Employee/
│   ├── Department/
│   ├── Attendance/
│   ├── Leave/
│   └── Payroll/
├── wwwroot/
