│   └── js/app.js
├── Program.cs
├── appsettings.json
└── EmployeeManagementSystem.csproj

---

FEATURES TO IMPLEMENT:

1. Authentication & Authorization
   - Login / Logout
   - Role-based: Admin, HR, Employee
   - Seed default Admin user on startup

2. Dashboard
   - Total Employees count
   - Department-wise breakdown
   - Pending Leave Requests
   - Today's Attendance summary
   - Recent activity feed

3. Employee Management (Full CRUD)
   - Add / Edit / Delete / View Employee
   - Fields: Name, Email, Phone, DOB, Gender, 
     Department, Designation, JoiningDate, 
     Salary, ProfilePhoto, Status (Active/Inactive)
   - Search + Filter by Department / Status
   - Pagination

4. Department Management (Full CRUD)
   - Department Name, Manager, Description
   - Employee count per department

5. Attendance Management
   - Mark attendance: Present / Absent / Half-Day
   - Filter by date range and department
   - Monthly attendance report per employee

6. Leave Management
   - Employee submits leave request (from-to date, reason, type)
   - Leave Types: Casual, Sick, Annual
   - HR/Admin: Approve / Reject with remarks
   - Leave balance tracker per employee

7. Payroll (Basic)
   - Auto-calculate based on Salary + Attendance days
   - Deductions: Absent days
   - Generate monthly payslip view per employee

---

DATABASE:
- Use SQLite for local dev (easy setup, no SQL Server needed)
- EF Core Migrations
- Seed data: 2 departments, 5 employees, 1 Admin user
- Connection string in appsettings.json

---

UI REQUIREMENTS:
- Dark sidebar layout (left nav)
- Clean Bootstrap 5 tables with action buttons
- Responsive (mobile-friendly)
- Toast notifications for success/error actions
- Modal popups for quick confirmations (delete)
- Status badges (Active = green, Inactive = red)
- Dashboard uses card widgets with counts

---

OUTPUT FORMAT:
- Provide complete file-by-file code
- Each file clearly labeled with its path
- Program.cs must include:
  * EF Core setup
  * Identity setup
  * Role seeding
  * Migration auto-apply on startup
- All Razor views must have proper @model directives
- Controllers must have [Authorize] with role filters
- All forms must use ASP.NET Tag Helpers
- No placeholder code — everything must be functional

---

OPENING INSTRUCTIONS (include at end):
1. dotnet restore
2. dotnet ef database update
3. dotnet run
4. Open https://localhost:5001
5. Default login: admin@ems.com / Admin@123
```

---

**How to use this:**

- Paste into Claude (new chat) or ChatGPT-4o
- It will generate file-by-file
- Copy each file into the correct folder in VS / VS Code
- Run the 3 commands at the bottom — project launches directly

**If you want to extend it later**, just append to the prompt: `"Also add: [feature]"` — the structure is modular enough to handle it cleanly.
